### II-A 3D Aerial Highway and ITNTN Architecture

As depicted in Fig. [1](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2607.18604v1#S2.F1 "Figure 1 ‣ II System Model ‣ Intelligent Multi-UAV Navigation in ITNTNs: A Hierarchical LLM Approach"), we consider a dynamic 3D aerial highway where a set of MM UAVs, denoted by ℳ={1,2,…,M}\mathcal{M}=\{1,2,\dots,M\}, navigate a shared airspace. Each UAV m∈ℳm\in\mathcal{M} is assigned an independent transit mission to a unique 3D target waypoint, 𝐱targetm\mathbf{x}\_{\text{target}}^{m}, and must continuously adjust its altitude and heading to bypass obstacles and avoid collisions.

