### IV-A HAPS Cloud Meta-Controller

At the highest level of the hierarchy, the HAPS acts as a global orchestrator. Since global load balancing requires complex spatial reasoning across the entire ITNTN, we deploy a large foundation model, i.e., Qwen3.5-122B, hosted in the cloud computing cluster of HAPS. Operating at THAPS=5.0T\_{\mathrm{HAPS}}=5.0 s, the HAPS meta-controller evaluates the global observation 𝐨THAPS\mathbf{o}\_{T}^{\mathrm{HAPS}}. In particular, if the number of users associated with a specific TBS nc,tn\_{c,t} is close to QcQ\_{c}, the LLM generates zero-shot strategic directives (𝐚THAPS\mathbf{a}\_{T}^{\mathrm{HAPS}}), forcing specific UAV edge-agents to offload their C2 links to neighboring TBSs or the HAPS.

