### IV-D State Discretization and Prompt Engineering

To bridge the gap between numerical kinematics and the semantic reasoning of the Qwen3.5-9B edge-LLM, we leverage a structured prompt engineering methodology. Directly feeding high-precision floating-point arrays (e.g., 𝐯tm=[12.43,−3.21,0.5]\mathbf{v}\_{t}^{m}=[12.43,-3.21,0.5]) often degrades LLM reasoning and inflates inference latency. Therefore, we discretize the continuous observation 𝐨tm\mathbf{o}\_{t}^{m} into semantic language descriptors, denoted as ℒ⁡(𝐨tm)\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{o}\_{t}^{m}). Specifically, the 3D relative distance to neighboring UAVs (‖𝐱tm−𝐱tj‖2\|\mathbf{x}\_{t}^{m}-\mathbf{x}\_{t}^{j}\|\_{2}, ∀j∈ℳ\{m}\forall j\in\mathcal{M}\backslash\{m\}) is categorized into predefined semantic zones: Safe (d>3​dsafed>3d\_{\text{safe}}), Warning (dsafe≤d≤3​dsafed\_{\text{safe}}\leq d\leq 3d\_{\text{safe}}), and Critical (d<dsafed<d\_{\text{safe}}). Similarly, the handover-aware network state WRtm,c\text{WR}\_{t}^{m,c} is mapped to Stable (when WRtm,c≥20\text{WR}\_{t}^{m,c}\geq 20 Mbps, indicating an un-congested link), Degraded (when 0≤WRtm,c<200\leq\text{WR}\_{t}^{m,c}<20 Mbps, indicating capacity saturation), or Hand-over (when WRtm,c<0\text{WR}\_{t}^{m,c}<0, triggered by the massive γ\gamma penalty during network switching).

